@@ -0,0 +1,37 @@
+# Visual review
+
+[`.github/workflows/visual.yml`](../.github/workflows/visual.yml) owns the complete capture and signed submission path. Pin that file's Git blob in Visonaut and in `VISONAUT_WORKFLOW_SOURCE_SHA`. Changes to app builds and deployment do not change this pin. Keep the exact CLI and adapter versions beside the digest in the pinned workflow. The adapter also belongs in the app manifest and lockfile. Signed Submit downloads its exact CLI version from the fixed HTTPS npm registry URL, verifies the tarball SHA256 before installation, and installs that local archive with scripts disabled in an isolated tools directory; the root no longer needs a CLI dependency. Update the reviewed CLI package digest with a package release.
+
+Ariakit owns page preparation, project selection, viewport and style variants, font readiness, and clip geometry. [`visual-reporter.ts`](../app/src/test-utils/visual-reporter.ts) keeps the repeated environment and reporter wiring in one local helper. Rendering identity contains measured operating system and font identity. The service owns comparison policy. Keep the bounded font and stable-pixel checks before capture.
+
+The `linux` job captures Chrome and Firefox. The `safari` job captures Safari. Each successful job uploads `manifest.json`, `environment.json`, and `images/` as `visonaut-capture-<run>-<attempt>-<shard>` for one day. Screenshots and retry traces used for failure diagnosis remain ordinary seven-day artifacts. Successful image attachment files stay outside that diagnostics folder.
+
+The candidate jobs have no OIDC or review authority. The signed Submit job checks out the trusted main toolchain and runs:
+
+```sh
+visonaut submit --shard linux --shard safari
+```
+
+Submit starts a pending App check before artifact work. It verifies the workflow, tested commit, real GitHub jobs, source attempts, expected artifacts, complete manifests, environment profiles, and image bytes. It forms a new complete bundle. A successful visual job that GitHub did not rerun can supply its verified source-attempt artifact. A rerun shard must supply fresh evidence. If an inherited one-day artifact expired, rerun the full visual set. The signed receipt also stays in CI for one day.
+
+The `Plan / Plan` job uses the same pinned workflow and runs the reviewed main planner for the tested base and head commits. The separate signed `Plan / Report` job waits for that successful job and reports its own exact output. An absent or invalid output fails before identity exchange. A caller cannot supply the visual decision. The service also verifies the successful Plan job, repository, exact run and attempt, tested commit, and approved workflow blob.
+
+Main pushes run a real Plan with `app=true` and all other workflow flags false. Its signed report completes before the existing main App pipeline starts. Pull requests retain the reviewed change planner. A verified `app=false` result completes the Visonaut App check promptly. A verified `app=true` result keeps it pending until complete signed evidence and review are available. An absent or failed Plan cannot pass. Gate checks ordinary CI. Its Plan dependency also includes the trusted report, so a failed report cannot pass Gate. Gate no longer polls for human review.
+
+## Coordinated cutover
+
+1. Publish and install the reviewed CLI and Playwright adapter versions that contain this protocol. Both planned pins are `0.4.0`. Test their packed contents, replace `PENDING_RELEASE_SHA256` with the actual reviewed CLI digest, and refresh the adapter lockfile from the published registry version. No registry resolution or integrity for the unpublished adapter is invented in this patch. The old encrypted-transfer package cannot run this workflow.
+2. Configure Visonaut to trust the new small workflow blob and the exact `Plan / Plan`, `Plan / Report`, `App / Visual / Capture / linux`, `App / Visual / Capture / safari`, and `App / Visual / Submit` jobs. Apply the Plan-check schema and handler before the consumer workflow starts.
+3. Require the `Visonaut` check from the Visonaut GitHub App beside `Gate`. Apply that rule with Gate's polling removal. Verify visual, no-visual, missing Plan, failure, cancellation, partial rerun, expired artifact, and same-commit rerun paths before closing the cutover.
+4. Read back the source pin, package digest, App rule, and a complete successful capture. Remove transfer secrets and obsolete endpoints only after no live reader needs them.
+
+This file defines the source contract. A source patch alone does not change a GitHub rule, publish a package, or update production configuration.
+
+Until the reviewed release exists, the adapter manifest and retained registry lock entry differ. A frozen install must fail. After publication is authorized and complete, run the following in the integration checkout, review the new registry integrity, and then run the normal frozen install and checks:
+
+```sh
+pnpm install --lockfile-only --ignore-scripts --no-runtime
+pnpm install --frozen-lockfile --ignore-scripts --no-runtime
+```
+
+The capture job also checks the installed adapter version before tests. The Plan report uses inline Node and installs no CLI archive. Signed Submit does not follow registry redirects, and a changed archive fails before package installation. Do not approve the source blob or start this workflow while the release digest marker or old adapter resolution remains.
